   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\nestablishing the Flax Pond tidal wetlands sanctuary; and to amend the\nnavigation law, in relation to prohibiting the use of motor boats in the Flax\nPond tidal wetlands sanctuary",
    "basePrintNo": "S9140",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9140-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §11-0306-a, En Con L; add §39-b, Nav L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9140\n\nSPONSOR: MATTERA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\nestablishing the Flax Pond tidal wetlands sanctuary; and to amend the\nnavigation law, in relation to prohibiting the use of motor boats in the\nFlax Pond tidal wetlands sanctuary\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo establish the- Flax Pond Tidal Wetlands Sanctuary to protect areas of\nspecial significance. The sanctuary shall be managed as a long-term\nfield laboratory for research.and education while also providing oppor-\ntunities for class instruction, public 'enjoyment, and protecting biodi-\nversity.\n\n \nSUMMARY:\n\nSection 1: Establishes the Flax Pond Tidal Wetlands Sanctuary delineat-\ning boundaries, management, and purpose.\n\nSection 2: Bans motor boats from being operated on the Flax Pond Tidal\nWetlands Sanctuary with certain exceptions and fines.\n\nSection 3: Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill protects the Flax Pond Tidal Wetlands providing a sanctuary\nfor local and regional biodiversity and opportunities for research,\neducation, and public enjoyment of nature.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the one hundred eightieth day after it\nshall have become a law.\n",
